---
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About | Eliham Pelaez"
	description="About Eliham Pelaez, Game Designer and Gameplay Programmer"
>
	<div class="stack gap-20">
		<main class="wrapper about">
			<Hero
				title="About"
				tagline="Thanks for stopping by. Read below to learn more about myself and my background."
			>
				<img
					width="1553"
					height="873"
					src={`${base}/assets/at-work.jpg`}
					alt="Eliham Pelaez at work"
				/>
			</Hero>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Background</h2>

				<div class="content">
					<p>
						I am a <strong>Game Design student and Gameplay Programmer</strong>
						passionate about creating interactive experiences and understanding how
						games can bring people together.
					</p>

					<p>
						My journey into game development began in third grade, inspired by my
						late father, who battled ALS. That experience shaped my determination
						to pursue a career in games and build experiences that can connect with
						people on a deeper level.
					</p>

					<p>
						By sixth grade, I was already teaching my classmates how to use
						<strong>Scratch</strong> and helping them understand programming logic.
						This early experience sparked my interest not only in programming, but
						also in <strong>teaching, collaboration, and communicating ideas to others</strong>.
					</p>

					<p>
						In seventh grade, I participated in the
						<strong>"Descubre-te"</strong> project in collaboration with the
						Sabaneta Mayor's Office. This was my first opportunity to work with
						<strong>Unity and C#</strong>, while also developing my teamwork and
						problem-solving skills in a collaborative environment.
					</p>

					<p>
						In 2018, I expanded my technical knowledge through a
						<strong>Game Development and Robotics</strong> summer course at EAFIT,
						where I created another game project and continued exploring
						programming and interactive media.
					</p>

					<p>
						In 2020, I decided to complement my technical skills with a
						<strong>Human Resources technician</strong> program. This experience
						helped me develop a stronger understanding of communication, teamwork,
						leadership, and how people interact within a working environment.
						These skills have become an important part of how I approach game
						development, particularly when working with multidisciplinary teams.
					</p>

					<p>
						I currently study <strong>Game Design at Universidad Pontificia
						Bolivariana (UPB)</strong>, where I work on projects involving games,
						animation, programming, and interactive experiences.
					</p>

					<p>
						In <strong>2026, I expanded my experience into Unreal Editor for
						Fortnite (UEFN)</strong> by completing the
						<strong>UEFN Bootcamp</strong>, where I developed projects using
						<strong>Verse</strong> and explored multiplayer gameplay development.
						This gave me hands-on experience building systems such as enemy
						management, round-based game modes, progression systems, interactive
						gameplay devices, and cooperative multiplayer mechanics.
					</p>

					<p>
						My experience across Unity, C#, UEFN, and Verse has allowed me to
						approach game development from both a
						<strong>design and technical perspective</strong>, with a particular
						interest in gameplay systems and interactive experiences.
					</p>

					<p>
						My goal is to continue growing as a
						<strong>game designer and gameplay programmer</strong>, combining
						technical knowledge with design thinking to create meaningful,
						engaging, and memorable experiences. I am particularly interested in
						developing gameplay systems that encourage player interaction and
						creating experiences where design and technology work together.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Education</h2>

				<div class="content">
					<p>
						<strong>B.A. in Game Design</strong> — Universidad Pontificia
						Bolivariana (UPB)
					</p>

					<p>Expected graduation: February 2027</p>

					<p>GPA: 4.3</p>

					<p>Epic Games UEFN Bootcamp — 2026</p>

					<p>Human Resources Technician — SENA, 2021</p>

					<p>Musical Introduction Certification — Atempo, 2019</p>

					<p>Game Development Summer Camp — EAFIT, 2018</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Skills</h2>

				<div class="content">
					<p>
						<strong>Game Development:</strong> Unity, Unreal Engine, UEFN,
						Gameplay Programming, Multiplayer Systems, Interactive Experiences.
					</p>

					<p>
						<strong>Programming:</strong> C#, C++, JavaScript, Verse,
						Pseudocode.
					</p>

					<p>
						<strong>Creative Coding:</strong> p5.js, Three.js, WebGPU.
					</p>

					<p>
						<strong>Interactive Media:</strong> OSC, TouchDesigner, Spout.
					</p>

					<p>
						<strong>Design:</strong> Game Design, Level Design, Gameplay Design,
						Art Direction, User Flows, Prototyping, Wireframing.
					</p>

					<p>
						<strong>Research:</strong> Qualitative User Research, Customer
						Interviews, Q/A, Customer Journey Mapping, Usability Testing,
						A/B Testing.
					</p>

					<p>
						<strong>Leadership:</strong> Design Thinking, User-Centered Design,
						Cross-Functional Collaboration, Communication and Storytelling,
						Agile Development Processes, Public Speaking.
					</p>

					<p>
						<strong>Tools:</strong> Excel, Word, Git, Git LFS, Notion, Miro,
						Clip Studio Paint, Aseprite, Illustrator, Animate, Maya, Figma,
						Photoshop, Arduino, Raspberry Pi, itch.io, Canva, Blender,
						TouchDesigner, Spout, OSC.
					</p>

					<p>
						<strong>Languages:</strong> Spanish (Native), English (Fluent C1).
					</p>

					<p>
						<strong>Interests:</strong> Video Games, Movies, Comics, Game Design,
						Music, Japanese Animation, Western Animation, Coding, Teamwork,
						and Helping People Grow.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>

		<ContactCTA />
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 3.5rem;
	}

	img {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
	}

	section {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		color: var(--gray-200);
	}

	.section-title {
		grid-column-start: 1;
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}

	.content {
		grid-column: 2 / 4;
	}

	.content :global(a) {
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
	}

	.content :global(a:hover),
	.content :global(a:focus) {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}

	@media (min-width: 50em) {
		.about {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 60% 1fr;
		}

		.about > :global(:first-child) {
			grid-column-start: 2;
		}

		section {
			display: contents;
			font-size: var(--text-lg);
		}
	}
</style>